Package: maplore
Title: Context Components That Help Readers Understand 'mapgl' Maps
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person("Juan Manuel", "Tocho", email = "11000056+JMTocho@users.noreply.github.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
Description: Adds components to 'mapgl' maps ('MapLibre GL JS' and
    'Mapbox GL JS') that put what the reader sees in context: a live
    summary of the features in view compared with the whole map, a ranking
    of the features in view, a tooltip that shows where each value stands
    among all of them, and a search box over the map's own data. Everything
    runs in the browser, so the components work in static HTML, 'R
    Markdown' and 'Quarto' documents without a 'Shiny' server.
